LOK: a JSON state ends the value a command sent before it

The callback queue drops a ".uno:X=value" state that repeats the last
value sent for X. A mixed selection is reported as JSON
({"commandName":".uno:X","dontcare":true}), which never touched that
record: after value, mixed, the same value again, the client was left
showing mixed. A redo that brings the value back after an undo into a
mixed selection did exactly that. A JSON state for a command now
forgets the value recorded for it, so the next one is sent.

--- a/desktop/source/lib/init.cxx
+++ b/desktop/source/lib/init.cxx
@@ -2546,6 +2546,15 @@
             }
             else
             {
+                // Ely: a JSON state ends the value sent before it.
+                static constexpr std::string_view aNamed = "{\"commandName\":\"";
+                if (type == LOK_CALLBACK_STATE_CHANGED && payload.startsWith(aNamed))
+                {
+                    const sal_Int32 nFrom = aNamed.size();
+                    const sal_Int32 nEnd = payload.indexOf('"', nFrom);
+                    if (nEnd != -1)
+                        m_lastStateChange.erase(payload.copy(nFrom, nEnd - nFrom));
+                }
                 const auto stateIt = m_states.find(type);
                 if (stateIt != m_states.end())
                 {
